From d2219a3ded9d91c8e727baa72f3b411890d087e7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Oleksii Zakharov <contact@zalexdev.com>
Date: Sat, 15 Aug 2026 18:56:54 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] um: fault around anonymous guest faults

A guest page fault is not expensive because of handle_mm_fault; it is
expensive because of the round trip. The stub takes SIGSEGV, hands the CPU
to the kernel thread, and a second handoff resumes it -- 18.9us in seccomp
mode and 41.0us under ptrace on the reference device, essentially all of it
those two voluntary context switches.

The stub's mmap transport is already batched: um_tlb_sync() walks the
marked PTE range and queues one stub syscall per page, and the queue is
executed in the same handoff that resumes the guest. Installing K extra
PTEs while we are already here therefore costs one handoff rather than K.

Restricted to vma_is_anonymous() && pte_none() && !userfaultfd_armed():
file faults can do I/O and have their own fault-around, a non-none PTE may
be a swap entry whose fault can block or return VM_FAULT_RETRY, and
userfaultfd has to see real faults. The window ramps 0 -> 4 -> 16 -> 32
pages behind a sequential detector, so random access never pays for pages
it will not touch. The cap is in bytes rather than pages ("prefault=",
default 128K, 0 disables) because PAGE_SIZE is parametric here -- a page
count would silently mean a 512K window on a 16K-page guest.

Measured on the same phone, medians of 7 interleaved rounds, validator at
0.7% and the native and proot control columns unchanged:

  fault, seccomp   18.891 us -> 10.749 us  (-43%)
  fault, ptrace    40.968 us -> 13.703 us  (-67%)

Every other row moved by less than 2%, which is what a change aimed at
faults should look like.

Signed-off-by: Oleksii Zakharov <contact@zalexdev.com>
---
 arch/um/include/asm/mmu.h   |  13 ++
 arch/um/include/shared/os.h |   1 +
 arch/um/kernel/skas/mmu.c   |   7 +
 arch/um/kernel/trap.c       | 249 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 arch/um/os-Linux/skas/mem.c |  19 +++
 arch/um/os-Linux/start_up.c |   1 +
 6 files changed, 290 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/um/include/asm/mmu.h b/arch/um/include/asm/mmu.h
index 07d48738b402b..e88b8155b70b4 100644
--- a/arch/um/include/asm/mmu.h
+++ b/arch/um/include/asm/mmu.h
@@ -21,6 +21,19 @@ typedef struct mm_context {
 	spinlock_t sync_tlb_lock;
 	unsigned long sync_tlb_range_from;
 	unsigned long sync_tlb_range_to;
+
+	/*
+	 * Anonymous fault-around state (arch/um/kernel/trap.c). A fault costs a
+	 * full stub handoff (~51us measured on-device in seccomp mode), so
+	 * sequential fault streams are detected and additional pages are
+	 * prefaulted into the same handoff. prefault_next is the page a
+	 * sequential stream would fault next (end of the last window);
+	 * prefault_level indexes the ramp. Purely a heuristic: fields are
+	 * accessed racily (READ_ONCE/WRITE_ONCE only) under mmap_read_lock,
+	 * a lost update just mispredicts one window.
+	 */
+	unsigned long prefault_next;
+	unsigned int prefault_level;
 } mm_context_t;
 
 #define INIT_MM_CONTEXT(mm)						\
